<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Mixed bids, slower movement.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Mixed bids, slower movement.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mixed and cash movement was slow, merchandisers in the High Plains said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Dealers said there had been an increase in activity Monday before the Kansas City Board of Trade opened.</p>
<p>&quot;It started out busy but then it just died when the market opened lower,&quot; a north central Oklahoma dealer said. &quot;It was one of the deadest days in a long time.&quot;</p>
<p>Another Oklahoma dealer estimated that around 70 percent of his state's crop had already been sold, which he said was about average for this time of year.  </p>
